<p><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isle_Royale_ridge_trail.jpg">The picture</a> is by Todd VerBeek, licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 4.0 International and found on Wikimedia Commons. (It's actually in Michigan, but I'd already written the details about BC.)</p>
<p>Originally this was pretty short with no logs, but Moklin advised I make it more of a story than a description. Overall I like how it turned out, although there are a few bits I'm not 100% satisfied with. (Specifically, if you drill down to the cave and then the person moves a bit, the shaft may not still be connected. And if it is, it'll be piercing a different part of their body&#8230;) Like a lot of anomalies, the mechanics start getting a little fuzzy if you inspect it from every angle. I ended up going with &quot;less is more&quot;, and it's good enough for jazz.</p>

